1
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:02,970
Listen, Hananoi-kun.

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,100
When I was in elementary school,

3
00:00:06,550 --> 00:00:13,610
this weird rumor went around that I had a 
crush on a boy that my friend liked.

4
00:00:13,890 --> 00:00:17,360
It wasn't true, of course, and I denied it.

5
00:00:17,360 --> 00:00:22,620
But I didn't try very hard to explain things
to my friend, and it really hurt her.

6
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:27,220
Is this the friend who cut your hair?

7
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:29,620
Yup.

8
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:33,660
We were so close, too.

9
00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:37,390
It made me realize that love
can change you, and that scared me.

10
00:00:38,210 --> 00:00:43,020
But I've always felt like if I'd understood 
what it meant to like someone,

11
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:47,140
maybe things would have 
turned out differently.

12
00:00:47,590 --> 00:00:51,290
The reason I wanted to date you
 and learn what love means

13
00:00:51,290 --> 00:00:53,410
was partly because of that.

14
00:00:55,960 --> 00:01:02,860
Hey, Hananoi-kun, doesn't the idea that 
you or I might change someday scare you?

15
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:12,830
For me, before I started dating you, 
food was just sustenance in my eyes.

16
00:01:13,620 --> 00:01:17,850
You taught me how delicious it can be.

17
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:23,360
If love has the power to change
 people for the worse,

18
00:01:23,730 --> 00:01:26,930
it must also have the power 
to change us for the better.

19
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:29,860
That's what I realize when I watch you.

20
00:01:34,510 --> 00:01:37,570
S-Say, Hananoi-kun...

21
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:47,240
Maybe you won't want this
since we baked our own.

22
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:51,760
But I really like you, Hananoi-kun.

23
00:01:52,460 --> 00:01:55,920
I'm... in love with you!

24
00:03:28,270 --> 00:03:34,560
Episode 7

25
00:03:28,270 --> 00:03:34,560
My First Confession

26
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:38,780
Thank you.

27
00:03:42,730 --> 00:03:44,080
I'm...

28
00:03:45,920 --> 00:03:47,010
so happy.

29
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:52,450
Are you sure about this?

30
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:57,940
Are you sure what you're feeling is love?

31
00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:08,010
Well, Kyo-chan says that love means 
different things for different people.

32
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:13,240
So it might not be the 
exact same thing you feel,

33
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:16,590
but I do think this is love!

34
00:04:19,160 --> 00:04:21,860
You know, I really do like you.

35
00:04:22,270 --> 00:04:24,070
I want to be with you all the time.

36
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:25,620
Uh-huh.

37
00:04:26,150 --> 00:04:29,740
As long as I have you,
 I don't care about anyone else.

38
00:04:30,150 --> 00:04:32,200
I don't need family or friends.

39
00:04:32,750 --> 00:04:33,630
Huh?

40
00:04:35,540 --> 00:04:40,000
I always want to be close to you, 
and I don't want to let anyone else near.

41
00:04:41,060 --> 00:04:44,940
I want all of you all to myself.

42
00:04:48,140 --> 00:04:52,610
Knowing that, do you still
 think you can love me?

43
00:04:57,070 --> 00:04:58,510
Gosh, it sure is cold!

44
00:05:00,390 --> 00:05:02,560
Oh dear. Is somebody home?

45
00:05:06,080 --> 00:05:09,050
Didn't you say you were going out today?

46
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:10,580
Grandma.

47
00:05:10,580 --> 00:05:12,070
H-How do you do?!

48
00:05:12,070 --> 00:05:13,330
My!

49
00:05:13,330 --> 00:05:16,760
What's this?! Did you sneak a girl in
to be alone together?

50
00:05:16,760 --> 00:05:18,620
I know your parents aren't around,

51
00:05:18,620 --> 00:05:21,410
but that doesn't mean you can just go wild!

52
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:24,470
I certainly hope you weren't 
doing anything naughty.

53
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:25,020
Huh?

54
00:05:25,020 --> 00:05:26,680
Don't say it like that.

55
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:29,210
D-D-Definitely not!

56
00:05:29,210 --> 00:05:32,210
Um, we were only baking 
chocolate cake together!

57
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,660
Chocolate cake?

58
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:37,100
Well, I do smell something nice.

59
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:40,820
U-Um, I'll be on my way.

60
00:05:40,820 --> 00:05:43,930
If you'd like, please try some.

61
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:47,540
Oh, wait. I'll walk you out.

62
00:05:49,220 --> 00:05:53,390
I'm sorry. My grandma is pretty 
strict about that kind of stuff.

63
00:05:53,980 --> 00:05:55,570
No, it's okay.

64
00:05:56,980 --> 00:05:59,440
Oh no! The train's coming!

65
00:05:59,440 --> 00:06:00,860
Hurry up!

66
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:01,620
Hotaru-chan!

67
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:03,150
Wait for me!

68
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:09,210
Th-Thank you.

69
00:06:11,790 --> 00:06:14,720
H-Here is fine. Thanks for walking with me.

70
00:06:16,560 --> 00:06:17,490
Sure.

71
00:06:18,030 --> 00:06:19,980
Hey, Hotaru-chan.

72
00:06:20,330 --> 00:06:23,380
Maybe we shouldn't talk for a while.

73
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:24,120
Huh?

74
00:06:25,130 --> 00:06:29,480
I want you to think seriously 
about what I said today.

75
00:06:30,040 --> 00:06:34,130
Once you've made up your mind, 
we can pick up where we left off.

76
00:06:34,490 --> 00:06:37,630
B-But I really do...

77
00:06:38,010 --> 00:06:40,750
It's okay. I know.

78
00:06:56,590 --> 00:06:58,060
Oh man...

79
00:06:58,770 --> 00:07:02,070
There you go again, 
trying to act like a good kid.

80
00:07:03,620 --> 00:07:08,280
When you really want something, 
why don't you just say so?

81
00:07:08,730 --> 00:07:11,020
Sometimes you should just be honest,

82
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:13,060
sonny.

83
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:18,410
I'm such an idiot.

84
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:25,410
<i>Think seriously about it, huh?</i>

85
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:30,450
<i>As long as I have you,
 I don't care about anyone else.</i>

86
00:07:31,200 --> 00:07:34,870
<i>I want all of you all to myself.</i>

87
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,470
<i>All of me?</i>

88
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:44,310
Hananoi

89
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:44,310
Let's stop walking to school
and eating lunch together
for a while

90
00:07:40,930 --> 00:07:44,310
Call received

91
00:07:44,310 --> 00:07:47,070
The Next Day

92
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,080
Hotako.

93
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:51,690
Oh!

94
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:54,480
What's up? You keep looking around.

95
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:56,250
Oh, um, it's nothing.

96
00:07:59,710 --> 00:08:01,440
<i>He really didn't come.</i>

97
00:08:02,390 --> 00:08:05,700
<i>He's stopped messaging me every day, too.</i>

98
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,120
Hananoi!

99
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:12,650
Oh?

100
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:15,990
I'll never ask you for anything else!
 Help me study!

101
00:08:15,990 --> 00:08:17,520
Why me?

102
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,220
Hell no.

103
00:08:19,780 --> 00:08:22,100
But you're super smart, right?

104
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:26,620
If I don't do better this school year, 
they'll drop me from the starting lineup!

105
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:29,800
Come on, Hananoi! I'm begging you!

106
00:08:32,460 --> 00:08:37,180
Wait. Isn't today the day you 
always eat with Hananoi-san?

107
00:08:38,550 --> 00:08:39,710
Yeah...

108
00:08:45,650 --> 00:08:46,560
Oh!

109
00:08:46,610 --> 00:08:49,050
<i>Can you pick something up for me?</i>

110
00:08:46,670 --> 00:08:50,420
Can you grab something at the
4-chome supermarket?

111
00:08:54,390 --> 00:08:55,710
Ugh.

112
00:08:56,420 --> 00:09:01,440
<i>Um, she also wanted... salad dressing?</i>

113
00:09:02,270 --> 00:09:03,190
There it is!

114
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:04,860
Oh!

115
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:04,860
Oh!

116
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:06,220
I'm sorry!

117
00:09:04,860 --> 00:09:06,220
I'm sorry!

118
00:09:06,220 --> 00:09:07,050
Huh?

119
00:09:07,050 --> 00:09:10,230
Oh my, it's you! The girl from before.

120
00:09:10,230 --> 00:09:11,560
You're Hananoi-kun's...

121
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:15,630
My name is Hinase Hotaru! 
I apologize for the other day!

122
00:09:16,310 --> 00:09:18,310
Not at all. I should apologize to you.

123
00:09:18,310 --> 00:09:21,560
I shouldn't have snapped at you 
like that. I'm sorry, dear.

124
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:22,390
Oh.

125
00:09:23,010 --> 00:09:25,330
I didn't realize it at the time,

126
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:29,520
but you're who called 
me last year, aren't you?

127
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:36,650
You left before I could thank you 
properly. It's been bothering me.

128
00:09:37,590 --> 00:09:39,840
So once again, you have my gratitude.

129
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:42,560
I-It was nothing.

130
00:09:43,150 --> 00:09:47,090
Say, do you live near here too, Hinase-san?

131
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:48,600
Huh? Yes.

132
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:53,050
In that case, might I have 
a bit more of your time?

133
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:03,700
It's getting cold, dear.

134
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:05,520
Oh, right!

135
00:10:13,250 --> 00:10:14,830
Oh, I see.

136
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:19,240
You've baked together and visited
a shrine with friends...

137
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:25,040
I suppose this means that boy is 
enjoying a normal high school life.

138
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:26,730
That's quite a relief.

139
00:10:27,150 --> 00:10:31,150
You know, he never tells me anything at all.

140
00:10:31,150 --> 00:10:33,230
I-Is that right?

141
00:10:33,690 --> 00:10:37,050
If it turned out he was living 
an unhealthy lifestyle,

142
00:10:37,050 --> 00:10:40,400
I was thinking of dragging 
him back to live with me.

143
00:10:41,650 --> 00:10:44,940
Why does Hananoi-kun live alone now?

144
00:10:44,940 --> 00:10:48,860
Oh, didn't he tell you? About his parents?

145
00:10:48,860 --> 00:10:52,450
He said they're doctors who work overseas.

146
00:10:53,340 --> 00:10:55,470
Well, it's not exactly work.

147
00:10:56,470 --> 00:10:58,290
They're practically volunteers.

148
00:11:01,310 --> 00:11:04,970
You see, his parents travel back 
and forth to poor countries,

149
00:11:04,970 --> 00:11:09,630
helping children who can't 
afford medical treatment.

150
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:12,990
I saw a show about people like that on TV!

151
00:11:15,100 --> 00:11:18,360
Well, what they're doing <i>is</i> wonderful,

152
00:11:18,360 --> 00:11:25,040
except they go around helping other peoples' 
children while ignoring their own son.

153
00:11:26,110 --> 00:11:28,920
I took care of him
while he was living with me.

154
00:11:28,920 --> 00:11:31,510
I wonder if he was embarrassed by that.

155
00:11:31,830 --> 00:11:36,630
Once he started high school, he wanted 
to move back into the old apartment alone.

156
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:41,280
He's a good boy, but he can be
 a bit extreme sometimes.

157
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:42,310
Yeah.

158
00:11:43,430 --> 00:11:46,260
Though he's changed a little recently.

159
00:11:47,770 --> 00:11:51,780
He never seemed to care 
much for food before,

160
00:11:51,780 --> 00:11:56,920
but now he asks me about cooking
 and even cleans his plate.

161
00:11:58,400 --> 00:12:00,770
I wonder who
is having an effect on him.

162
00:12:00,770 --> 00:12:01,700
Huh?

163
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:10,110
By the way, what happened to your hand?

164
00:12:10,600 --> 00:12:12,290
Oh, this little thing?

165
00:12:12,650 --> 00:12:16,710
When I went over to cook for him, 
I goofed and burned myself.

166
00:12:17,030 --> 00:12:23,060
I told him it'd heal on its own, 
but he dragged me to the hospital.

167
00:12:23,060 --> 00:12:26,020
It isn't such a big deal. Don't worry, okay?

168
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:32,980
Hananoi

169
00:12:30,980 --> 00:12:32,980
Let's stop walking to school
and eating lunch together for a while

170
00:12:36,870 --> 00:12:40,260
<i>I'm good just holding one person truly dear.</i>

