H-Hananoi-kun?

192
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:13,960
<i>Ah! Hotaru-chan?</i>

193
00:14:15,470 --> 00:14:19,960
<i>Sorry to surprise you. 
I got your message.</i>

194
00:14:20,880 --> 00:14:23,100
O-Oh, yeah.

195
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:26,870
<i>So, actually, right now...</i>

196
00:14:44,410 --> 00:14:47,060
Sorry. I'm here.

197
00:14:52,290 --> 00:14:53,480
Hotaru?

198
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:55,680
Where are you going at this hour?

199
00:14:55,680 --> 00:14:56,870
Just the convenience store!

200
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,320
Hananoi-kun!

201
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:21,890
Oh! S-Sorry!

202
00:15:21,890 --> 00:15:24,730
I've been so Hotaru deprived, 
I wasn't thinking!

203
00:15:28,850 --> 00:15:31,930
Me too! I've missed you so much!

204
00:15:37,760 --> 00:15:38,840
So...

205
00:15:39,370 --> 00:15:42,300
I'm positive I like you, Hananoi-kun.

206
00:15:42,970 --> 00:15:47,300
But when you ask if I'm sure about it,

207
00:15:47,300 --> 00:15:51,420
I'm not sure I can keep up with 
you on all your sense of values.

208
00:15:51,420 --> 00:15:54,760
I'm not confident I'll be an ideal girlfriend.

209
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:59,190
I mean, I don't have any reason 
whatsoever to be confident.

210
00:16:00,320 --> 00:16:01,380
But you know...

211
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:07,770
Can't we still be together, 
even if we see things differently?

212
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:18,190
The other day when we were baking 
together, I was so happy.

213
00:16:19,670 --> 00:16:21,480
But it wasn't just then.

214
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,480
There have been so many occasions

215
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:28,410
that were a delight.
Where I was thrilled to be with you,

216
00:16:29,280 --> 00:16:31,710
or even just to talk to you.

217
00:16:33,390 --> 00:16:38,190
I figure maybe, as those things keep 
adding up, I'll find my confidence.

218
00:16:41,450 --> 00:16:45,280
So, you know, I think this 
is just the beginning.

219
00:16:46,700 --> 00:16:48,920
I want it to be you, Hananoi-kun.

220
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:54,040
Things may not always work,
 and I might cry sometimes,

221
00:16:54,040 --> 00:16:56,390
but you're who I want to share that with.

222
00:16:58,810 --> 00:17:03,250
So do you think you could go out
 with someone like me?

223
00:17:08,520 --> 00:17:12,600
That's what... I should be asking you.

224
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:16,030
What? Why are you crying?

225
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:17,970
I'm not crying.

226
00:17:17,970 --> 00:17:21,120
Oh, really? Sorry, my mistake.

227
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:31,380
I'm sorry. I'm the one lacking confidence.

228
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,850
<i>He really is crying.</i>

229
00:17:43,160 --> 00:17:44,290
I love you.

230
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:50,960
Y-You flatter me.

231
00:17:54,490 --> 00:17:56,140
I'm looking forward to us.

232
00:17:56,560 --> 00:17:58,980
So... So am I!

233
00:18:04,150 --> 00:18:07,660
<i>D-Does this mean we're about toâ€”</i>

234
00:18:31,540 --> 00:18:33,380
<i>It's winter. I'm sixteen.</i>

235
00:18:34,220 --> 00:18:38,690
<i>And starting today, we really 
are boyfriend and girlfriend.</i>

236
00:20:28,990 --> 00:20:31,940
The Horse and the Witch

237
00:20:31,050 --> 00:20:32,010
Hey there.

238
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:37,120
All by yourself again, sonny?

239
00:20:42,090 --> 00:20:46,850
What's going on? You look 
even gloomier than normal.

240
00:20:47,750 --> 00:20:53,680
My mom and dad promised to 
come back to Japan next week,

241
00:20:53,680 --> 00:20:55,350
but now they can't.

242
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:57,400
Is that right?

243
00:20:58,640 --> 00:21:03,620
Well, a doctor's life is 
always full of surprises.

244
00:21:03,610 --> 00:21:09,620
The Horse and the Witch

245
00:21:03,980 --> 00:21:09,300
I wonder if even they care about me at all.

